meta {
  name: Share Order Report
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/order/{{orderId}}/share
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "channel": "EMAIL",
    "toAddress": "patient@example.com"
  }
}

docs {
  "Share and Inform" from the Order Console: queue the order's lab report to the
  patient over one channel, using the tenant's ACTIVATED
  `console_lab_report_as_attachment` template (no template picker).

  - `channel` (required): `EMAIL` | `SMS` | `WHATSAPP`.
  - `toAddress` (optional): destination override; when omitted, the patient's
    stored email (EMAIL) / whatsappNumber||mobile (WHATSAPP) / mobile (SMS) is used.

  Email/WhatsApp attach the rendered `lab_all_report` PDF (base64); SMS is text-only.
  Requires: an activated messaging template for the channel + feature, AND an
  active `lab_all_report` PDF template for the tenant (so the report can render).

  Errors: 422 `SHARE_TEMPLATE_NOT_ACTIVATED` (no activated template for the channel),
  400 `SHARE_RECIPIENT_MISSING` (no address/number), 404 `ORDER_REPORTS_NOT_FOUND`.
  Returns the queued communication_logs row(s); the worker delivers via Exchange.
}
